pool space, their share of the party's damage, healing done, damage taken) plus the party's accounting line, and /bosstrial stats (public, like the status view) re-shows the caller's most recent fight record read back from the fights/ files, always with the full split - player damage, other damage, the pool the boss healed back, and the net the verdict judged on - so a fight's accounting is visible to the players who fought it; the healing column ships in this build because the 0.4.0 Protect healing-attribution proof passed (the gate the design held it behind), chat for Java and a Floodgate form for Bedrock throughout. 0.5.1 is the seal fight-feel Packet B (Item 35; the separate 0.5.0 voice packet is a different lane and is NOT in this jar - this build carries no voice features. At the dragon's phase flip the trial re-lights four end crystals on bare towers (never more than six live trial crystals), so the skyline changes and phase 2 re-opens the crystal game; the dragon's elite sprinkle is armed and cadence-driven in phase 2 only (180s, four elite endermen a wave, ten alive, forty a fight), fountain-anchored from battle registration, and the chapter's private Sealbound enderman waves are retired in the same step; when an elder of a monument trio is counted (one or two of three), the monument answers - each surviving elder with an open fight owes a sprinkle wave and fires its milestone surge under a broadcast line; and every player-facing pool-space number (per-hit feedback, totals, the stats pop-up, boss-bar pool figures) renders at a uniform display scale (feedback.display-scale, default 1000) so the vanilla gear ladder stays visible after each chapter's intake factor (wooden, diamond and netherite hits read as three plainly different, plainly ordered values) - display only, the ledger and governor math are unchanged.
